          "role": "assistant",
          "content": "To choose a committee of 3 members from 10 members, the order of selection does not matter.\n\nSo we use combinations.\n\nThe number of ways to choose 3 members from 10 is:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{3}=\\frac{10!}{3!(10-3)!}\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{3}=\\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1}\n\\]\n\nNow calculate:\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 9 \\times 8 = 720\n\\]\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 6\n\\]\n\n\\[\n720 \\div 6 = 120\n\\]\n\nSo there are 120 different ways to choose the committee.\n\nAnswer: 120",
